19	{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "forgetful-leray-base-term-vanishes", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0036", "equivalence_group": "forgetful-leray-base-term-vanishes", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0019", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "obstruction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "For the forgetful map M_{g,n} -> M_{g,n-1} used at an open input in ordinary degree D=2d-k, the Leray E_2 term E_2^{D,0}=H^D(M_{g,n-1};Q) vanishes whenever D exceeds the vcd of the base, which is the case at (6,6) with D=26 and base vcd 25. The two-row spectral sequence then degenerates to an isomorphism H^D(M_{g,n}) = H^{D-1}(M_{g,n-1};R^1 pi_* Q) with no differentials. Consequently any argument of the form 'the base summand is Tate by published CKgP for n-1' is vacuous, and this style of forgetful reduction transports the entire difficulty into local-system cohomology without reducing it. Future attempts using this route should be required to state the vanishing explicitly rather than presenting the base term as discharged progress.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
20	{"adjudication_reason": "No claim-level contradiction: contradicts_claim_ids is empty, and the statement does not oppose CONJ-0001, THM-0001\u2013THM-0007, OBS-0001, or RED-0001. It is compatible with THM-0001 (pure HS only for smooth proper stacks) and with the forgetful-Leray bookkeeping already used by sibling findings FND-0015/FND-0027 (extension 0\u2192H\u2192R^1f_*Q\u2192Q(-1)^{m-1}\u21920) and FND-0036 (H^D(M_{g,n})\u2245H^{D-1}(M_{g,n-1};R^1\u03c0_*Q) at the open-input degree). Primary MHS check: for C smooth projective of genus g and S a set of m\u22651 points, Deligne\u2019s theory yields the SES of MHS 0\u2192H^1(C;Q)\u2192H^1(C\\S;Q)\u2192Q(-1)^{m-1}\u21920, so Gr^W_1 has rank 2g (weight 1) and Gr^W_2 has rank m-1 (weight 2, Tate). For the universal n-punctured curve one has m=n, hence Tate rank n-1 as stated; pure weight 1 holds only for n\u22641. For the campaign case (g,n)=(6,6), L=R^1\u03c0_*Q along M_{6,6}\u2192M_{6,5} (or the universal 6-punctured system) therefore has weights \u22651, so H^p(base;L) has weights \u2265p+1; at p=2d\u2212k\u22121=25 one has lowest weight 26 and W_25=0, so any pure-corner label W_p at that spot is the zero group. Mild scope sharpening only: absolute \u2018never pure of weight 1\u2019 is for m\u22652 (n\u22652 universal, n\u22653 forgetful); the (6,6) instance and the ATT-0011 error-pattern warning remain intact. Distinct from FND-0037/FND-0027 (non-split extension obstructing graded splitting of Leray terms) and from FND-0014 (uncontrolled symplectic local-system cohomology): do not merge. Promote from candidate to corroborated on independent primary-source verification of the mixed-weight structure and weight-floor consequence; evidence_class upgraded from legacy_artifact to primary_source. ATT-0011 section-level provenance was not re-audited (artifact absent from the read-only workspace) and is not required for the mathematical promotion.", "adjudication_status": "decided", "adjudicator": "FAUD-0002", "candidate_