{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "open-input-degree-equals-vcd", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0035", "equivalence_group": "open-input-degree-equals-vcd", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0017", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "structural", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "The RED-0001 base-case inequalities coincide with the virtual cohomological dimension boundary for M_{g,n}. For n>=2 the condition k>=2g-2+n is equivalent to 2d-k<=4g-4+n with d=3g-3+n, and for n<=1 the condition k>=2g is equivalent to 2d-k<=4g-6; that is, the ordinary realization degree of every unresolved open input lies at or one below the vcd (for (6,6): degree 26 equals vcd 26; for (6,5): vcd 25). Any forgetful-Leray or stratification route therefore has its higher-degree terms killed for free, and top-degree tools rather than local-system evaluations are the natural attack. Corroboration needed against a primary source for Harer's vcd formula, which is not in the packet corpus.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_reason": "Church-Farb-Putman does not prove arbitrary-puncture top-vcd vanishing.", "adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "top-degree-vanishing-may-settle-open-input", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "equivalence_group": "top-degree-vanishing-may-settle-open-input", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0018", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "candidate-resolution", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "Because the ordinary realization of the (6,6) open input sits exactly at the vcd, a top-degree rational vanishing theorem for mapping class groups (H^{vcd}(M_{g,n};Q)=0 for g>=2, as in the Church-Farb-Putman line of work) would give W_26 H^26(M_{6,6};Q)=0 and hence W_{-16}H^BM_16(M_{6,6})=0, which is vacuously a direct sum of copies of Q(8) and would discharge this pair outright. This is flagged as a line to verify, not as an established input: no such theorem appears in the supplied packet, its exact hypotheses at n>0 must be checked, the g=0 case is a known counterexample, and the top-degree group is coinvariants of a Steinberg-type dualizing module, so invariants-versus-coinvariants must be handled explicitly. Requires independent source verification before any attempt relies on it.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "forgetful-leray-base-term-vanishes", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0036", "equivalence_group": "forgetful-leray-base-term-vanishes", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0019", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "obstruction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "For the forgetful map M_{g,n} -> M_{g,n-1} used at an open input in ordinary degree D=2d-k, the Leray E_2 term E_2^{D,0}=H^D(M_{g,n-1};Q) vanishes whenever D exceeds the vcd of the base, which is the case at (6,6) with D=26 and base vcd 25. The two-row spectral sequence then degenerates to an isomorphism H^D(M_{g,n}) = H^{D-1}(M_{g,n-1};R^1 pi_* Q) with no differentials. Consequently any argument of the form 'the base summand is Tate by published CKgP for n-1' is vacuous, and this style of forgetful reduction transports the entire difficulty into local-system cohomology without reducing it. Future attempts using this route should be required to state the vanishing explicitly rather than presenting the base term as discharged progress.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_reason": "No claim-level contradiction: contradicts_claim_ids is empty, and the statement does not oppose CONJ-0001, THM-0001\u2013THM-0007, OBS-0001, or RED-0001. It is compatible with THM-0001 (pure HS only for smooth proper stacks) and with the forgetful-Leray bookkeeping already used by sibling findings FND-0015/FND-0027 (extension 0\u2192H\u2192R^1f_*Q\u2192Q(-1)^{m-1}\u21920) and FND-0036 (H^D(M_{g,n})\u2245H^{D-1}(M_{g,n-1};R^1\u03c0_*Q) at the open-input degree). Primary MHS check: for C smooth projective of genus g and S a set of m\u22651 points, Deligne\u2019s theory yields the SES of MHS 0\u2192H^1(C;Q)\u2192H^1(C\\S;Q)\u2192Q(-1)^{m-1}\u21920, so Gr^W_1 has rank 2g (weight 1) and Gr^W_2 has rank m-1 (weight 2, Tate). For the universal n-punctured curve one has m=n, hence Tate rank n-1 as stated; pure weight 1 holds only for n\u22641. For the campaign case (g,n)=(6,6), L=R^1\u03c0_*Q along M_{6,6}\u2192M_{6,5} (or the universal 6-punctured system) therefore has weights \u22651, so H^p(base;L) has weights \u2265p+1; at p=2d\u2212k\u22121=25 one has lowest weight 26 and W_25=0, so any pure-corner label W_p at that spot is the zero group. Mild scope sharpening only: absolute \u2018never pure of weight 1\u2019 is for m\u22652 (n\u22652 universal, n\u22653 forgetful); the (6,6) instance and the ATT-0011 error-pattern warning remain intact. Distinct from FND-0037/FND-0027 (non-split extension obstructing graded splitting of Leray terms) and from FND-0014 (uncontrolled symplectic local-system cohomology): do not merge. Promote from candidate to corroborated on independent primary-source verification of the mixed-weight structure and weight-floor consequence; evidence_class upgraded from legacy_artifact to primary_source. ATT-0011 section-level provenance was not re-audited (artifact absent from the read-only workspace) and is not required for the mathematical promotion.", "adjudication_status": "decided", "adjudicator": "FAUD-0002", "candidate_key": "punctured-curve-local-system-is-mixed-not-pure", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "equivalence_group": "punctured-curve-local-system-is-mixed-not-pure", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0020", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "error-pattern", "reviewer_engines": ["claude", "grok"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "R^1 pi_* Q for the universal n-punctured curve is mixed of weights 1 and 2 (an extension of a rank n-1 Tate system of weight 2 by the rank 2g weight-1 system), never pure of weight 1. The correct weight floor is therefore H^p(base;L) of weight >= p+1, so at p=2d-k-1 the relevant graded piece is Gr^W_{p+1}, and any 'W_p' group named at that spot is identically zero. Attempts that describe the punctured-curve system as pure of weight 1 will be off by exactly one unit of weight and will target a zero group. ATT-0011 exhibits this error in section 2 while stating the correct description in section 5.", "status": "corroborated", "supporting_artifact_hashes": ["b48d8e91facddbfec194b1f3015f119b9cf522402bc241cf12f2bbce2ed4efb6"], "supporting_audit_ids": ["FAUD-0002"], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_reason": "Contradicts cross-checked THM-0005, whose scope is open M_g,n.", "adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "ckgp-compact-to-open-pure-weight-gap", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "equivalence_group": "ckgp-compact-to-open-pure-weight-gap", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0021", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "obstruction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "Invoking the published CKgP marking bounds to conclude that an open pure-weight group W_{2m}H^{2m}(M_{g,n}) is a sum of Q(-m) skips two steps that must be argued rather than asserted: CKgP is a property of the smooth proper compactification, and the lowest-weight part of the open cohomology is the image from a smooth compactification, so one needs both the compact-to-open comparison and the implication algebraicity implies Hodge-Tate for a pure weight-2m structure. ATT-0011 section 3 asserts the composite in one line and marks it 'proved'. Any attempt using THM-0005 to Tate-ify open pure-weight cohomology should be required to exhibit these two steps.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_reason": "No claim-level contradiction: contradicts_claim_ids is empty, and the statement does not oppose CONJ-0001, THM-0001\u2013THM-0007, OBS-0001, or RED-0001. It is compatible with THM-0005 (c(6)=5, so n=6 lies outside published CKgP range and stratification/Gysin assembly is a natural residual method) and with sibling FND-0020/FND-0036 forgetful-Leray bookkeeping (the base local-system contribution still requires stratified assembly on M_{6,5}). Independent primary checks. (1) Hyperelliptic codimension: dim M_g=3g-3 and dim H_g=2g-1 (Pries arXiv math/0601596 \u00a72.1), so codim(H_6\u2282M_6)=(3\u00b76-3)-(2\u00b76-1)=4 as claimed; the same codimension persists for the hyperelliptic locus in M_{6,5}. Standard Thom\u2013Gysin/localization for a smooth closed immersion of pure codimension c supplies the contribution H^{p-2c}(stratum)(-c)\u2245H^{p-8}(H_6)(\u22124) with Tate twist Q(\u22124), so the stated shift/twist bookkeeping is correct; differentials of the localization spectral sequence must still be controlled. (2) Restriction to the open stratum is neither injective nor surjective in general by the localization long exact sequence (support cohomology of the closed strata intervenes), so evaluating only the open gonality stratum cannot bound pure-weight pieces of H^*(total; L). (3) Gonality range for g=6: Brill\u2013Noether gives generic gonality \u230a(g+3)/2\u230b=4, so smooth genus-6 curves realize only gonality values 2,3,4 (hyperelliptic, trigonal, tetragonal); there is no residual gonality-5 stratum. SRC-0004/Canning\u2013Larson (arXiv 2208.02357v2 \u00a7\u00a78\u201310) explicitly stratify by gonality M^k_{g,n} for k=2,3,4 and, in genus 6, identify a further Brill\u2013Noether-special plane-quintic locus PQ\u2282M_6 inside the tetragonal (gonality-4) open: smooth plane quintics have genus 6 and gonality 4 (projection from a point) while carrying a g^2_5 with \u03c1(6,2,5)=\u22123<0. Residual BN specializations are therefore refinements inside a single gonality stratum, not separate gonality strata\u2014matching the mislabelling clause. Distinct from FND-0031/FND-0034 (Deligne weight spectral sequence of the Deligne\u2013Mumford boundary, depth-one Gysin from codimension-one strata) and from FND-0020 (mixed weights of R^1\u03c0_*Q): do not merge. ATT-0011 shift/twist provenance was not re-audited (artifact absent from the read-only workspace) and is not required for the mathematical promotion of the obstruction. Promote from candidate to corroborated; evidence_class upgraded from legacy_artifact to primary_source. Merge target: none.", "adjudication_status": "decided", "adjudicator": "FAUD-0003", "candidate_key": "gonality-stratification-lacks-gysin-assembly", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "equivalence_group": "gonality-stratification-lacks-gysin-assembly", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0022", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "obstruction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude", "grok"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0011"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0018"], "statement": "A gonality or Brill-Noether stratification of M_{g,n-1} does not by itself bound the pure-weight cohomology of a local system on the total space: one needs the localization spectral sequence with the correct codimension shifts and Tate twists (in genus 6 the hyperelliptic locus has codimension 4 in M_6, contributing via degree p-8 cohomology of the stratum twisted by Q(-4)) together with control of its differentials. Evaluating only the open stratum is insufficient, since restriction to it is in general neither injective nor surjective. ATT-0011 supplies no shift, twist, or differential bookkeeping, and its stratification is additionally mislabelled: for g=6 gonality takes only values 2, 3, 4, the posited residual Brill-Noether strata are not separate gonality strata, and the gonality-4 open contains the Brill-Noether-special plane quintic locus.", "status": "corroborated", "supporting_artifact_hashes": ["ff89841ffa4bbca1c248eff833b556525aa7eea2d7e9588bcb17df540d7cac56"], "supporting_audit_ids": ["FAUD-0003"], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "harer-vcd-punctured-formula", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0035", "equivalence_group": "harer-vcd-punctured-formula", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0023", "impacts_approach_ids": ["prove-pure-weight-tate-only"], "kind": "correction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0012"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0019"], "statement": "Harer's virtual cohomological dimension for mapping class groups is vcd(Mod_{g,n}) = 4g-4+n for g>=1, n>0, and 4g-5 only for g>=2, n=0 (with n-3 for g=0, n>=3). The interpolated form 4g+n-5 used in ATT-0012 is the n=0 formula illegitimately extended and understates the vcd by exactly 1 for every n>=1; independent check: Mod_{1,1} = SL_2(Z) has vcd 1 = 4-4+1, not 4+1-5 = 0. For (g,n)=(6,6) the correct value is 26, so no vanishing is available in ordinary degree 26.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "red0001-pairs-sit-at-or-below-vcd", "case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0035", "equivalence_group": "red0001-pairs-sit-at-or-below-vcd", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0024", "impacts_approach_ids": ["prove-pure-weight-tate-only"], "kind": "obstruction", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 6, "n": 6}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0012"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0019"], "statement": "No cohomological-dimension argument can discharge any open input in the RED-0001 list. With the correct Harer vcd, the gap vcd(Mod_{g,n}) - (2d-16) for d=3g-3+n equals 18-2g-n when n>=1 and 17-2g when n=0, which is 0 for (3,12), (5,8), (6,6), (7,4), (8,2) and 1 for (8,0), (8,1). Hence the required ordinary degree 2d-16 never exceeds the vcd for any listed pair, and lands exactly on it for five of the seven: the reduction's unresolved inputs sit at the very top of the virtual cohomological dimension, which is structurally why they are hard. Any future attempt whose engine is degree-based vanishing (vcd, affineness, or homotopy-dimension bounds) can be rejected on arithmetic alone without examining its Hodge theory.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
{"adjudication_status": "decided", "candidate_key": "open-input-sits-in-vcd-degree", "case": {"g": 5, "n": 8}, "contradicts_claim_ids": [], "created_on": "2026-07-30", "duplicate_of": "FND-0035", "equivalence_group": "open-input-sits-in-vcd-degree", "evidence_class": "legacy_artifact", "id": "FND-0025", "impacts_approach_ids": ["exact-point-count-or-equivariant-stratification"], "kind": "structural_observation", "reviewer_engines": ["claude"], "scope": {"case": {"g": 5, "n": 8}}, "source_attempt_ids": ["ATT-0013"], "source_review_ids": ["REV-0020"], "statement": "For every RED-0001 entry with n>=2 the extremality k=2g-2+n=16 forces 2g+n=18, hence the ordinary realization degree 2d-16=6g+2n-22 equals Harer's vcd(M_{g,n})=4g-4+n exactly: (3,12)->20, (5,8)->24, (6,6)->26, (7,4)->28, (8,2)->30; the n=0,1 entries (8,0)->26 and (8,1)->28 sit at vcd-1. The open input is therefore top-degree (or next-to-top-degree) rational cohomology of the open moduli, well above its complex dimension. If the known vanishing of H^{vcd}(M_{g,n};Q) for g>=2 applies, the open input is zero, hence trivially a (empty) direct sum of Q(8), and the entire point-count/monodromy program is unnecessary. The vcd input is reviewer-supplied and outside the dependency-closed corpus; this must be corroborated against a citable source before use.", "status": "retired", "supporting_artifact_hashes": [], "verification_method": "revision-2 adversarial review"}
